      "id": "soyuz-apollo-crews",
      "path": "assets/cover-film/soyuz-apollo-crews.jpg",
      "caption": "Экипажи «Союза — Аполлона», 1975. NASA",
      "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_ASTP_crews_-_restoration.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/Portrait_of_ASTP_crews_-_restoration.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "downloadUrl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Portrait_of_ASTP_crews_-_restoration.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_ASTP_crews_-_restoration.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
      "author": "Adam Cuerden",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "licenseUrl": "",
      "sha256": "8fbdef9c0eba0061764edebeb2dc2592b76842de59db8a49c66e3ba1557a2b1b",
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 1024,
      "bytes": 308903,
      "description": "S75-22410 (March 1975) --- These five men compose the two prime crews of the first-ever two-nation cooperative space mission, known in the US as the Apollo-Soyuz Test Project (ASTP) and in the Soviet Union as the Soyuz-Apollo Experimental Flight (Russian: Экспериментальный полёт Союз-Аполлон, Eksperimantalniy polyot Soyuz-Apollon).  This was a docking mission in Earth orbit scheduled for July 1975. They are astronaut Thomas P. Stafford (standing on left), commander of the American crew; cosmonaut Aleksey A. Leonov (standing on right), commander of the Soviet crew; astronaut Donald K. Slayton (seated on left), docking module pilot of the American crew; astronaut Vance D. Brand (seated center), command module pilot of the American crew; and cosmonaut Valeriy N. Kubasov (seated on right), engineer on the Soviet crew. \nThe crew members wear the same mission patch, but oriented to reflect \"Soyuz-Apollo\" or \"Apollo-Soyuz\", as the program was called in their respective countries.",
      "changes": "Thumbnail; original color retained. Used under independent animated masks."
    }
